    </p>

    <h2>4. Local-first product; your providers</h2>
    <p>
      Codescribe processes speech on your Mac by default. Optional features may
      send text or audio to providers you enable (for example AI formatting,
      agent tools, or cloud STT). Those providers have their own terms and
      privacy policies. You are responsible for keys, usage limits, and content
      you send them. See the <a href={page('privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to use the App to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Violate law or third-party rights</li>
      <li>Attempt unauthorized access to systems or data</li>
      <li>Abuse, harass, or generate illegal content via agent features</li>
      <li>Circumvent license checks, sandboxing, or security controls</li>
